{
  "version": "0.6.1",
  "notes": "Fix real data corruption found on first successful cellular test: this modem's firmware splits large AT+HTTPREAD responses into multiple '+HTTPREAD: DATA,<n>' chunks (observed: a 3522-byte manifest came back as 4 chunks of up to 1024 bytes each), not the single-marker shape assumed in 0.6.0's parse_http_read(). The old parser only stripped the FIRST chunk's marker line, leaving later chunks' marker lines embedded as literal garbage and silently dropping real content -- caused 'syntax error in JSON' on the very first real OTA check after cellular connectivity was confirmed working. Also: cellular.py now always resets the modem before the first AT command (previously an opt-in flag that defaulted to False, almost certainly why every earlier attempt got zero response from the modem before it was even powered).",
